      "content": "i get what u mean about the speed of change. but when we're looking at these transition zones, there's often a pattern where certain types of ethnic or immigrant communities taking up residential space can lead to changes in the types of businesses that open up, like more informal economy stuff or shops that don't fit the \"standard\" commercial model. from a bank perspective, is there a way to quantify how these specific cultural or ethnic shifts impact the perceived stability of a commercial corridor?",
