      "content": "From a bank perspective, you typically quantify these impacts by analyzing granular debt metrics, such as occupancy rates, default frequencies, and payment history variations among new demographic cohorts within that corridor. Since ethnicity and culture do not directly alter creditworthiness or loan performance, relying solely on codes that breach this demographic framing would be inappropriate and could introduce unnecessary bias into your risk models. Instead, your assessment should focus on how the specific *speed* of transition interacts with the economic trajectory of the area, rather than attributing commercial instability directly to cultural or ethnic shifts.",
